    <td align="right" valign="top" nowrap><b>Subject:</b></td>
    <td align="left" colspan="2" valign="top">Gyroscopic Propulsion, Good or Bad?</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td align=right class=medium valign="top" nowrap><b>Question:</b></td>
    <td align=left class=medium valign="top" width="400" colspan="2">I'm trying to wrap my mind around just how true gyroscopic propulsion would change our world. The obvious benifits that come to mind are: possible end to fuel crisis, faster and further travel postential, cleaner envirenment.<br>
<br>
Are there any negative effects such a discovery could have on our world? For some reason it almost seems like such an invention does seem right -- but I don't know why. Could it just be because it seems to be breaking the rules of physics? <br>
<br>
Curious to know what you guys think about this beyond the wanting to do it/see it/understand it stage.<br>
<br>
<br>
Thanks,<br>
<br>
Shawn<br>
</td>
  </tr>
